    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-ceiling platoon advantages, headlined by **Mickey Moniak**, who leads our lineup with a 74.96 score. His matchup against Sonny Gray is bolstered by a significant park factor (+14%) and a favorable platoon shift (+14%), making him our premier option. Following closely, **Corbin Carroll** (71.26) remains an elite start against Leahy, while **Josh Naylor** (68.78) anchors the corner infield against Mitch Keller, benefiting from a soft 4.45 xERA matchup and a solid boost from the fourth spot in the order. We are also banking on **Brice Turang** (64.65) to capitalize on a favorable offensive environment, despite facing the southpaw Lodolo, as his second-spot placement and high-speed upside keep his efficiency elevated above the 60-point threshold.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Zach McKinstry** on the bench with a 52.58 score. While his platoon edge against Rod\u00f3n was encouraging, the density of our current starters\u2014specifically the high-upside deployment of **Travis Bazzana** at the top of the order\u2014pushed him just outside the active roster. We are closely monitoring the status of **James Wood**; his 54.45 score is depressed by a daunting matchup against Jesus Luzardo, whose elite strikeout profile and 3.41 xERA create significant risk. However, **Wood**\u2019s elite 0.404 xwOBA keeps him in the lineup, as we prioritize his plate appearances despite the difficult statistical environment. Elsewhere, **Seiya Suzuki** (62.92) is a confirmed start, though we have factored in a minor penalty for the opponent\u2019s ability to suppress stolen bases, a crucial consideration given our organizational obsession with efficiency in that category. **Trevor Story** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving our middle infield depth to rely heavily on the production of **Alex Freeland** and **Max Muncy** to navigate today's varied pitching matchups.",
